AI was used for the commit message and code comments.

This along with !42653 are the 2 changes from common code KosmicKrisp needs to expose Vulkan 1.4 once we wrap up the last few things.

```
spirv: record float-controls preservation requests in shader_info

Signed zero, Inf and NaN preservation is tracked per ALU instruction
through nir_fp_math_control, but those bits mix shader requests with
spec-mandated semantics and lowering artifacts: ordered comparisons
receive the inf/nan bits in every shader, helpers such as nir_atan2
set preserve bits internally, and the signed-zero bit is dropped on
ops where it is meaningless.

Backends that translate NIR into another source language with only
translation-unit-level fast-math control (e.g. Metal, where fast math
breaks NaN comparisons and Inf quantization) instead need to know
whether the shader declared the SignedZeroInfNanPreserve execution
mode, or requested preservation through shader_float_controls2's
FPFastMathDefault execution mode or FPFastMathMode decorations. Only
spirv_to_nir sees those declarations, so record them in
shader_info::float_controls_execution_mode.

Unlike the original composite bits, each reinstated bit is set when
preservation of at least one of the three controls is requested at
the given float width. Only explicit shader requests are recorded:
the OpenCL environment's implicit preserve default seeded for kernels
is not, and the per-instruction path records solely from
FPFastMathMode-decorated instructions so builder defaults cannot leak
across float widths (defaults are recorded once, by the execution
mode handlers).

This partially reverts commits 9da2d218041 ("vtn: implement default
fp_math_ctrl without using execution mode") and 5e8cc19a3ba ("nir:
remove per shader float fast math flags"): the builder-local state
feeding the per-ALU bits is kept, the shader_info recording is
reinstated alo
